# The scaling by a of a ball with 2-limb center, with the special states of a ball:
# ball_scale_2, then the fix-up of milestone1.md, "Ball kernels".
# One ball operand, so q is rx itself; |cz0| is named az here, since a is the operand.
kernel:        ball_scale_2_full
input:         cx = cx0 cx1
input:         stored rx
input:         a
output:        cw = cw0 cw1
output:        rw
value:         cx*a
requires:      ball cx rx
ensures:       encloses cw rw x*a x=cx,rx
min_precision: 2
source:        ball_scale_2, then the fix-up of the special states of a ball (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       core: as ball_scale_2; fix-up: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeBallCores.v ball_scale_2_full_correct
entry:         yes
ieee_only:     yes
cone_exempt:   the fix-up selects, after explicit tests that the center and the radius are finite (f) and that no operand is empty (e); B1 to B4 of milestone1.md, "Ball kernels", state what comes out

(cz0, cz1, rz) = ball_scale_2(cx0, cx1, rx, a)
e              = eq(rx, rx)
az             = abs(cz0)
f1             = lt(az, const inf)
f2             = lt(rz, const inf)
f              = and(f1, f2)
c0             = select(f, cz0, 0)
c1             = select(f, cz1, 0)
r              = select(f, rz, const inf)
cw0            = select(e, c0, rx)
cw1            = select(e, c1, rx)
rw             = select(e, r, rx)
